<% provide(:title, "DID Linter") %>
<% example_did = "did:oyd:zQmZZbVygmbsxWXhP2BH5nW2RMNXSQA3eRqnzfkFXzH3fg1" %>

<section class="intro">
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">DID Linter</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    DID Linter resolves a decentralized identifier, or takes a DID document, and checks it against
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/">Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) v1.0</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="stack">
  <section class="card" id="did">
<% if DidLint.offline? -%>
    <h3>Check a DID</h3>
    <p>This instance runs in offline mode and makes no outgoing connections, so it cannot resolve DIDs.
      Paste the DID document below instead.</p>
<% else -%>
    <%= form_with url: validate_path, method: :get, class: "check", local: true do |form| %>
      <%= form.label :did, "Check a DID" %>
      <div class="row">
        <%= form.text_field :did, value: @did.to_s, placeholder: "did:method:identifier", spellcheck: false, autocomplete: "off" %>
        <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Check</button>
        <button class="btn secondary" type="submit" formaction="<%= root_path(anchor: "document") %>">Show document</button>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        <code>did:oyd</code> is resolved through the <a href="https://resolver.ownyourdata.eu">OYDID resolver</a>,
        all other methods through the <a href="https://dev.uniresolver.io">Universal Resolver</a>.
        Example: <a href="<%= validate_path(did: example_did) %>"><code><%= example_did %></code></a>
      </p>
    <% end %>
<% end -%>
<% if @result && @source == :did -%>
    <%= render "results", anchor: "did-result" %>
<% end -%>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="document">
    <%= form_with url: validate_path(anchor: "result"), class: "check", local: true do |form| %>
      <%= form.hidden_field :did, value: @did.to_s %>
      <%= form.label :did_document, "Check a DID document" %>
      <%= form.text_area :did_document, id: "did_document", value: @did_document.to_s, spellcheck: false,
            placeholder: "{\n  \"@context\": \"https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1\",\n  \"id\": \"did:example:123\",\n  …\n}" %>
      <div class="row">
        <button class="btn primary" type="submit" name="commit" value="Validate">Check document</button>
        <button class="btn secondary" type="submit" name="commit" value="Reset">Clear</button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
<% if @result && @source == :document -%>
    <%= render "results", anchor: "result" %>
<% end -%>
  </section>
</div>

<h2>How DID Linter checks</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Structure.</strong> The document is validated with SHACL against the
      <a href="<%= soya_structure_url %>">SOyA structure</a> for DID documents: required members, identifier
      syntax, verification methods and their key material, verification relationships and services.</li>
    <li><strong>Context.</strong> For a JSON-LD document, the <code>@context</code> is checked against the
      verification method types the structure lists, with the contexts the
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/did-spec-registries/#verification-method-types">DID Specification Registries</a> name for them.</li>
    <li><strong>Result.</strong> Each problem is listed with the member of the document it concerns, for example
      <code>verificationMethod</code>. Notes that do not change the result, such as a suggestion to add a
      JSON-LD context, are shown separately.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">Results come from automated checks only. They are not a certification, and the structure does
    not yet cover every requirement of DID Core.
<% if DidLint.offline? -%>
    This instance runs offline and validates against its local copy of the structure.
<% end -%>
  </p>
</div>

<% if (status = method_status) -%>
<h2 id="methods">DIF-recommended methods</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <p>Every day DID Linter checks example DIDs of the methods that the Decentralized Identity Foundation
    <a href="https://github.com/decentralized-identity/did-methods/tree/main/dif-recommended">recommends</a>,
    and of <code>did:oyd</code>.</p>
  <ul class="methods">
<% status[:methods].each do |m| -%>
    <li>
      <div class="method"><% if m[:link] %><a href="<%= m[:link] %>"><code><%= m[:method] %></code></a><% else %><code><%= m[:method] %></code><% end %></div>
      <div class="dids">
<% m[:dids].each do |d| -%>
<% css, label = method_status_badge(d) -%>
        <div class="did">
          <span class="badge <%= css %>"><%= label %></span>
          <div class="ref">
            <a href="<%= validate_path(did: d[:did]) %>" title="<%= d[:did] %>"><code><%= d[:did] %></code></a>
<% if (detail = method_status_detail(d, status[:generated])) -%>
            <span class="detail"><%= detail %></span>
<% end -%>
          </div>
        </div>
<% end -%>
<% if m[:note] || m[:dids].empty? -%>
        <p class="detail"><%= m[:note] || "No example DID yet." %></p>
<% end -%>
      </div>
    </li>
<% end -%>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">Last checked <%= status[:generated].utc.strftime("%-d %B %Y, %H:%M UTC") %><%= " with DID Linter #{status[:version]}" if status[:version] %>.
    A result describes the example DIDs listed in
    <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint/blob/main/status/methods.json">status/methods.json</a>,
    not every DID of a method.</p>
</div>
<% end -%>

<h2>Use it elsewhere</h2>
<div class="grid">
  <article class="card">
    <h3>REST API</h3>
    <p>Validate a DID or a posted DID document; every path is described in Swagger.</p>
    <pre><code>curl https://didlint.ownyourdata.eu/api/validate/<%= example_did %></code></pre>
    <div class="links"><a href="/api-docs/index.html">API documentation</a></div>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>Command line</h3>
    <p>The same checks with <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/soya">soya-cli</a> and two scripts from the repository.</p>
    <pre><code>cat did.json | script/prep.sh | soya validate <%= soya_did_dri %>
cat did.json | script/verify_context.rb</code></pre>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint/blob/main/script/prep.sh">prep.sh</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint/blob/main/script/verify_context.rb">verify_context.rb</a>
    </div>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>Your own instance</h3>
    <p>Run the Docker image yourself, online or fully offline with a local copy of the structure.</p>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/oydeu/didlint">oydeu/didlint</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint#offline-mode">Offline mode</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<h2>Building blocks</h2>
<div class="grid">
  <article class="card">
    <h3>SOyA</h3>
    <p>Semantic Overlay Architecture: data models in YAML with overlays for validation and
      transformation. The rules of DID Linter are a SOyA structure, published from
      <a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint/blob/main/soya/Did.yml"><code>soya/Did.yml</code></a>.</p>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://soya.ownyourdata.eu">soya.ownyourdata.eu</a>
      <a href="https://ownyourdata.github.io/soya/">Documentation</a>
    </div>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>OYDID</h3>
    <p>The <code>did:oyd</code> method of OwnYourData: identifiers derived from the hash of the DID
      document, with a hash-linked log of all changes.</p>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://oydid.ownyourdata.eu">oydid.ownyourdata.eu</a>
      <a href="<%= validate_path(did: example_did) %>">Check an example</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<h2>Source code and feedback</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <ul class="repos">
    <li><a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint">didlint</a><span class="what">This service – Rails, runs stand-alone or offline</span></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/soya">soya</a><span class="what">SOyA – structures, validation and transformation</span></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/oydid">oydid</a><span class="what">OYDID – the did:oyd method</span></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/OwnYourData/didlint/issues">Issues</a><span class="what">Report a wrong verdict or a missing rule</span></li>
  </ul>
</div>
